# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — written BEFORE any download or generated output exists.
#
# Rationale: GSE230649 alone is 8.6 GB of bedGraph. A single accidental commit
# of a large file is painful to remove from history and may exceed GitHub's
# hard 100 MB per-file limit. Data are reproduced by download scripts +
# checksum manifest, never by version control. Git LFS is deliberately NOT
# used (free-tier quota is too small for this volume).
#
# Policy: data directories are excluded wholesale, then specific small,
# human-authored metadata files are re-included with '!' exceptions.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Data — excluded wholesale
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/**
data/processed/**

# Keep the directory structure in a fresh clone so scripts do not fail on
# missing paths. .gitkeep files are the only thing tracked inside them.
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/.gitkeep

# data/metadata/ IS tracked — it holds small, hand-curated or script-emitted
# provenance files (manifests, checksums, sample sheets). Guard it anyway:
data/metadata/**/*.rds
data/metadata/**/*.RData
data/metadata/**/*.h5

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Genomics file formats — blocked ANYWHERE in the tree (belt and braces)
#    These catch a stray download into the repo root or a scripts/ subdirectory.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bedGraph
*.bedgraph
*.bg
*.bw
*.bigWig
*.bigwig
*.wig
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.crai
*.sam
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fa.gz
*.2bit
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.gtf
*.gtf.gz
*.gff
*.gff3
*.narrowPeak
*.broadPeak
*.gappedPeak
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.h5
*.h5ad
*.loom
*.rds
*.RDS
*.RData
*.rda
*.qs
*.feather
*.parquet

# Re-include tiny tracked exceptions if ever needed (none at present):
# !config/example_small.rds

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Archives and bulk downloads
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.7z
# GEO supplementary bundles
*_RAW.tar
GSE*_RAW*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Large intermediates and results objects
#    results/tables/ (CSV/TSV) and figures/ ARE tracked — they are deliverables.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/objects/**
!results/objects/.gitkeep
cache/
.cache/
tmp/
temp/
scratch/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. R / renv
#    renv.lock IS tracked (it is the reproducibility contract).
#    The package library is NOT — it is restored from the lockfile.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/lock/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/
renv/staging/
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj.user
.Renviron.local

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Quarto / knitr / rendered output caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.quarto/
*_cache/
*_files/
!docs/*_files/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md
/_site/
/_book/
/_freeze/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Logs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/**
!logs/.gitkeep
*.log
!docs/**/*.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Python (only relevant if the optional arboreto/GRNBoost2 path is taken)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.Python

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Credentials — must never be committed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Renviron
.env
*.pem
*.key
!*.pub
secrets/
credentials*
token*
!config/*.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. OS and editor cruft
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Scratch runner scripts at repo root
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway shell wrappers used to drive R from the Windows host without the
# PowerShell/WSL quoting traps (see docs/research_journal.md). They are execution
# scaffolding, not analysis: nothing here is needed to reproduce a result, and
# one was committed by accident before this rule existed. Anything that IS needed
# to reproduce a result belongs in scripts/ with a number and a header.
#
# ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist. The first version of this rule named the prefixes in
# use at the time (/.commit_*, /.run_*) and was immediately outgrown — a later
# batch of .check_*, .test_* and .probe_* wrappers was committed by accident
# because none of them matched. Enumerating scratch prefixes is a losing game, so
# every dot-file at the repo root is ignored and the legitimate ones are named.
/.*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.Rprofile
!/.github/          # CI workflows — the allowlist above would otherwise hide them
